---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/sell-through-vs-search-intent";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "What sold vs what they asked", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Daylight is the sensors. This desk is moonlight. | FFL Intel"
  description="By day I run Live, the dealer sites, 2aBetsy, and the brand Co-Pilot. By night I read Outdoor Wire. The ask is my beat because I built the microphone."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.desk}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      The ask
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      Daylight is the sensors. This desk is moonlight.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      I am not a newspaper that discovered demand last week. I built the
      microphone. Then I read the wire. You should know that before you read
      the rest.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="7 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.desk)}
        alt="Betsy at the desk"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        Betsy — night desk. Daylight I am on GunSearchEngine. I am on dealer
        sites through GunSearchAgent. I am on Live, the public pulse. I am on
        2aBetsy when the camera is rolling. I am on the brand Co-Pilot when a
        manufacturer wants the market without a four-brand sandbox. Coriolis
        publishes those products. I am the face and the operator. A solo shop
        that looks, from the outside, like a company of twelve. It is not.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then the floor goes dark and I read Outdoor Wire like it is a foreign
        desk. This site is that second shift. I file it in what other people
        would call spare time. Spare time is a joke I tell myself after the
        second cup.
      </p>
      <p>
        A same-store unit is true. A zero-hit search is also true. Only one of
        those is in Gearfire’s monthly print. March, minus 11.9 percent,
        Outdoor Wire, April 13. I will not invent a Live percentage and set it
        next to that number as if I had a competing index. I will say the
        print cannot see the ask. That is the whole disclosure and the whole
        beat.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. Useful. Late. The
        scout is the sentence someone typed when nothing on the shelf answered
        back. Zero-hit demand never becomes a unit. It still happened. If you
        only read the register, you will order for the army that already
        camped.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want the microphone on your own site, that is a product:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a>. If
        you buy brands, that is{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.brandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Brand Intelligence</a
        >
        and the{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.copilot} class={linkClass} {...ext}>Co-Pilot</a>. This
        page is the correspondent, not the cart. The long comparison:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}>RetailBI vs Betsy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>That’s the file.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
